// The package's own tests.
//
// A separate config so the base one keeps `"types": []`. That is not tidiness:
// an empty ambient type set is what makes `process` or `Buffer` in a core
// source file a compile error rather than something the gate has to catch by
// pattern. The tests legitimately need node's, so they get their own config
// instead of relaxing the rule for everything.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["src", "test"]
}
